{"id":"efb3c389-6918-4fff-8028-9d825d507978","object":"chat.completion","created":1785006331,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    # Build edges with mutual reachability\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n        edges.append((mr, u, v))\\n    # Sort by weight then by first endpoint then second endpoint\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    # Union-Find\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    # Input is guaranteed connected for public fixtures; if not, this would still produce MST\\n    return {\\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges, \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight}\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write solve(case) that given payload with nodes, core_distance dict, and distances list (each entry [node1, node2, distance]), computes mutual reachability MST using Kruskal's algorithm. Output must be dict with \"mst_edges\" (list of [node1, node2, weight]) and \"total_weight\" (sum of weights). Must be deterministic: tie-breaking by reachability then endpoint IDs. Use union-find.\n\nImportant: Input case payload may have _case_nonce but we ignore. Use nodes, core_distance, distances.\n\nAlgorithm: Build all edges: for each distance entry, compute mutual_reachability = max(core_distance[node1], core_distance[node2], distance). Then create edge (node1, node2, mutual_reachability). Canonicalize: sort node1<node2? Actually canonicalize undirected endpoints: store as sorted tuple (min, max). Then sort edges by (mutual_reachability, node1, node2). Then Kruskal: initialize UnionFind dict mapping node to parent. For each edge in sorted order, if find(u) != find(v), union them, add to mst_edges, add weight to total. If we add n-1 edges, break. When done, check if we have exactly n-1 edges (otherwise disconnected). Return mst_edges list (each as [node1, node2, weight]) and total_weight.\n\nHandle floating point numbers: use float.\n\nThe output schema requires mst_edges items to have prefixItems [string, string, number]. So that's fine.\n\nImplementation details: Use recursion for find with path compression. Union by rank not required but good.\n\nWrite solve(case) that takes the inner payload object. No need to access outer keys.\n\nNow produce Python source as JSON string in {\"implementation\": \"...\"}. Escape newlines, quotes, backslashes. Make sure it's valid JSON inside.\n\nI'll implement.\n\nEdge case: duplicates? Not expected. But we treat distances list as all pairs. Ensure we don't miss any. Also ensure we only process each pair once.\n\nNow write the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1987,"completion_tokens":893,"total_tokens":2880,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":446},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":67},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}